    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald is delighted to present Rosaria, 31 Grosvenor Road, to the market. This is a truly handsome and substantial Victorian residence which dates back to c.1874. Spanning three generations of the same family this home has been under their custodianship for almost a century. Rosaria is superbly positioned in one of Dublin 6's most sought-after and mature residential locations only a light stroll away from Rathgar & Rathmines villages. Full of character and beautifully proportioned throughout, boasting an abundance of period features, the property offers generous and versatile accommodation laid out over three floors.\n\nA flight of gracious granite steps leads to this elegant red brick two-storey over garden home to the hall door complete with fanlight and ornate plasterwork surround. Inside, original fine adorning period features and elegant rooms of generous proportions combined with all the conveniences of modern living to create a really superb family-friendly home.\n\nAt hall floor level, a welcoming entrance hall leads to a bright living room and a generously proportioned dining room with a bay window, both reception rooms enjoying feature open marble fireplaces, high ceilings and ceiling cornices. A spacious kitchen/breakfast room lies at the heart of the home at garden level, complemented by a practical utility and store, while a wonderful conservatory to the rear enjoys views over and access to the garden.\n\nOn the hall level return, there is a guest WC and double bedroom facing the rear.\n \nOn the first floor lies an impressive and elegant drawing room/master bedroom enjoying fine proportions with feature marble fireplace. Another generous double bedroom and a shower room completes the accommodation at this level. The second floor is given over to a further spacious double bedroom with its own feature fireplace and en-suite shower room, offering a private and versatile retreat.\n\nThe private, southwest facing rear garden is landscaped in paving and gravel bordered by mature shrubs and specimen plants making it an ideal space for 'al fresco' dining. There is a pedestrian side access leading from the front to rear of the home in addition to double vehicular gates which offers the opportunity to install an electric car charger and a second pedestrian gate both opening to Leicester Avenue, accessed off Rathgar Road & Kenilworth Square South. \n\nThe location is second to none in terms of convenience, nestled between the villages of Rathgar and Rathmines, with every amenity on your doorstep to include excellent local shopping with a choice of fine restaurants. A large number of local junior and senior schools and Ashbrook Lawn Tennis Club are within an easy walk. The city centre and many of Dublin's principal places of business are within easy commuting distance from various bus routes a stroll away.\nAll in all, this is undoubtedly a genuinely special, truly stylish and unique family home situated in a highly desirable location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 9.56m x 2.11m\ntimber floors, dado rail, ceiling coving, fan light over door, decorative arch.\n\nDining Room - 5.50m x 4.16m\ntimber floor, bay window, feature open marble fireplace, tiled hearth, picture rail, ceiling coving, centre rose\n\nLiving Room - 3.41m x 4.51m\ntimber floor, picture rail, ceiling coving, centre rose, sash window to front with working shutters, open fireplace with gas fire inset.\n\nLower Hall - \ndoor to garden, tiled floor door to;\n\nUtility Room - 3.76m x 1.33m\nwindows to side, plumbed for washing machine & tumble dryer.\n\nKitchen - 6.34m x 4.51m\nwall & floor units, original range with granite surround. Sash window to rear.\n\nConservatory - 3.12m x 5.30m\ntiled floor, double glazed windows, double doors to garden, stained glass door to lower hall.\n\nReturn Landing - \narched window with stained glass, sash window, dado rail and ceiling coving\n\nGuest WC - \ntimber flooring and timber panels, sash window to rear with privacy glass, WC, wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.28m x 4.41m\ntimber floor, built in wardrobes, open fireplace, ceiling coving, sash window to rear.\n\nMain Bedroom / Drawing room - 4.35m x 6.94m\ntimber floor, picture rail, ceiling coving, centre rose, dual sash windows to front with working shutters, picture window to side.\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.45m x 3.82m\ntimber floor, ceiling coving, built in wardrobe, sash window to front, open fireplace.\n\nShower Room - \ntiled floor & walls, WC, wash hand basin, shower with glass screen. sky light, shower light.\n\n1st Floor landing - \ntiled floor and walls, corner shower, WC, wash hand basin and extractor.\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.40m x 3.36m\ntimber floor, ceiling coving, sash window to rear. Built-in wardrobes, open fireplace.\n\nEn suite Shower room - \ntiled floor and walls, corner shower ,WC, wash hand basin and extractor.\n\nFront Garden - \ncut stone granite wall with red brick piers and wrought iron pedestrian gate. Lawn and flower beds. Flight of granite steps leading to hall door.\n\nRear Garden - \npaved with border flower beds, pedestrian & vehicular gates to Leicester Avenue, cut stone granite walls, pedestrian side entrance to rear.\n\n"
